<title>NETHERLANDS: DSM 9-MONTH NET PROFIT NLG 591 MLN.</title>
<headline>DSM 9-MONTH NET PROFIT NLG 591 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HEERLEN, Netherlands 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996.</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit incl. extraordinary items     591  vs  927</p>
<p>    Ditto per share (guilders)		 19.68* vs  25.61</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charges			   10  vs  nil</p>
<p>* Calculated on the basis of ordinary shares outstanding at the</p>
<p>end of the period concerned.</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)			   7.67  vs  7.53</p>
<p>    Operating profit (billions)		 0.82  vs  1.35</p>
<p>    Interest charges				  42  vs  49</p>
<p>    Tax						  225  vs  428</p>
<p>The number of ordinary DSM shares outstanding at the end</p>
<p>of the nine-month period amounted to 29 million, compared with</p>
<p>36.2 million in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>The reduction is due to the conversion of 20 percent of</p>
<p>shares into cumulative preference shares on 12 March 1996.</p>
<p>The average number of shares outstanding over the period to</p>
<p>end-September 1996 amounted to 30.4 million.</p>
<p>Taking this as a base, the net profit per ordinary share was</p>
<p>18.78 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
